  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The flat circle motif relies on one rule: six "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "double-crochet-uk"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "double crochet"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " increases per round, staggered so they do not land in the same position twice. Stacking all increases in six columns produces a hexagon; staggering them round by round keeps the edge genuinely circular. Four rounds from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "magic ring"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " give a 12 cm disc in DK cotton on a 4 mm hook. The motif is the base component for many crocheted flat shapes: rugs, coasters, applique flowers, and the foundation round of beret crowns."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "infoPanel",
        "attrs": {
          "variant": "materials"
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Yarn: DK weight cotton, approximately 20 m per motif. Hook: 4 mm. Notions: tapestry needle, scissors, stitch marker (optional), blocking mat and pins (optional)."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "4 rounds in DK cotton with a 4 mm hook = 12 cm diameter. Gauge is not critical for a decorative motif, but a tighter tension produces a firmer, less pliable disc. If the circle cups, go up a hook size; if it ruffles, go down."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
